# elemental — Core Rules

Modular PyTorch ML training library. Config via Hydra; tracking via W&B. Uses `uv` for Python env, Docker for deployment.

## Import Convention
`src/` is on `PYTHONPATH`. Import as `from model.transformer import Transformer` — never `from src.model...`.

## Commands
```bash
uv run python src/trainer.py experiment/<task>/<config>
uv run python src/trainer.py ... key=value
uv run pytest tests/
uv run pre-commit run --all-files
```

## Hydra Configs
All configs live in `configs/` using hierarchical Hydra composition. Experiment configs in `configs/experiment/` compose sub-configs via `defaults:` lists. Entry point: `configs/config.yaml` → `configs/default.yaml`. Objects use `_target_` for instantiation.

## Unified Data Container
All components share a single `dict`. Keys: `input/<k>`, `target`, `pred`, `pred/<k>`, `post_processed/<k>`, `model`, `epoch`.
Never pass tensors directly between components — always use this container.

## Documentation
Every `src/` subdirectory has `README.md` (usage) and `ARCHITECTURE.md` (implementation).
**Update both files for every directory you modify.** Also update the outermost `README.md` and `ARCHITECTURE.md` if changes affect project-level docs. Outdated docs are worse than no docs.

## Planning
If a task has more than 3 steps, create a plan first before executing.

## Testing
Tests mirror `src/` structure under `tests/`. Add tests for new functionality only. Run `uv run pre-commit run --all-files` before committing.
